      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "From what was stated in the dev updates about this feature, this is sort of 'intended' behaviour.\n\nThe reason for this being that you can only have one world \"guaranteed preloaded\" at a time. Previously preloaded worlds are then unmarked as preloaded because they can get overwritten by other things in the cache and aren't \"protected\" from what I understand.\n\nThat being said, I still agree that this should change though. I think it's kind of a given that you can't expect all of your preloads to last forever. The most recent preload can still just be the \"guaranteed one\" while the others remain marked as preloaded. I feel like unmarking them when they're not actually gone from the cache is kind of confusing behaviour for both new and veteran players.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
